\pard\fi0\li0\tx705\tx1410\tx2130\tx2835\tx3540\tx4245\tx4950\tx5670\tx6375\tx7080\tx7785\tx8490\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 152\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 158\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Ps.-]Dionysius Areopagita: Epistulae\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , \u220 \'dcbersetzung von Johannes Sarracenus (Ep. 1\endash 10). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >Incipiunt epistole beati Dyonisii. Prima Gayo monacho.< Tenebre occultantur lumine et magis multo lumine \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 super omnia, que \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (152\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 cognoscuntur. >Eiusdem ad eundem. Secunda epistola.< Quomodo quidem super omnia et super thearchiam \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et participancium. >Eiusdem ad eundem iii epistola. Dubitacio \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [!] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 est, quod est preter spem \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et intellectum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [!] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ignotum. >Eiusdem ad eundem quarta epistola.< Quomodo, dicis, Ihesus, qui est super omnia \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (153\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 nobis conservatus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [!]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 . >Dorotheo dyacono, quid fit, quod dicitur:Posuit tenebras latibulum suum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [Ps 17,12]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 . Epistola quinta.< Divina caligo est inaccessibile lumen \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 est omnium causa existens. >Sosipatro sacerdoti sexta epistola.< Ne opineris hoc victoriam \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (153\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 esse irreprehensibilia que dicuntur. >Policarpo iherarche septima epistola.< Ego quidem non scivi \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [!] \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 adversus Grecos \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (153\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 religionis nostre veritatem. >Demophilo monacho de propria operacione et bonitate. Octava epistola.< Hebreorum historie dicunt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (156\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 credo eo esse vera. >Thito iherarche interroganti per epistolam, que est sapiencie domus, quis crather et qui cibi eius et qui potus. Epistola ix.< Sanctus quidem Thymotheus, o pulcherrime Tyte, nescio si aliquid cognitorum michi theologicorum signorum quod non audierit \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (158\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 sanctis tradicionibus et veritatibus. >Johanni appostolo et evangeliste exulanti in Pathma insula x epistola.< Saluto te, sanctam animam, o dilecte \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (158\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 post te trades. >Appollophano concreto et conphilosopho amico suo a cultu solis iam ad fidem Christi converso undecima epistola.< Nunc michi sermo ad te dirigitur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 cum ipse in eo vivens. >Expliciunt epistole beati Dyonisii undecim.< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash  Druck: Epistulae 1\endash 5 und 9: Dionysiaca, s.o., Bd. 2, S. 605\endash 669; Epistulae 6\endash 8 und 10: Dionysiaca, s.o., Bd. 4, S. 1479\endash 1578. Epistula 11 (nicht zum Corpus Dionysiacum geh\u246 \'f6rig): GW 8409 (nicht eingesehen); dazu P. Lehmann, Zur Kenntnis der Schriften des Dionysius Areopagita im Mittelalter, in: ders., Erforschung des Mittelalters, Bd. 4, Stuttgart 1961, S. 128\endash 141, hier S. 136. CPG Nr. 6604\endash 6613 mit Suppl. und Nr. 6630. Weitere Angaben vgl. Bl. 15\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .}

