\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 190\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 198\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 vb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [{\field{\*\fldinst HYPERLINK "hida://bezwrk[0].6930/?u"}{\fldrslt \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26\chcbpat17 Anonymi Teutonici commentum in Eclogam Theoduli}}\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 ]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , Exzerpt. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ethiopum terras iam fervida torruit estas, In cancro solis dum. Aristoteles: Effectus ille non est bonus, cuius cause legitime non precesserunt. Idcirco circa presentis operis inicium primo videndum est de causis. Pro quo notandum, quod quatuor sunt cause sciencie huius libelli, scilicet materialis, formalis, efficiens et finalis. Unde causa materialis sive subiectum communiter ponitur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (198\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Venit ab octeano \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [!]. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Hic Pseustis ponit aliam fabulam \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 usque ad mortem Christi durantes\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Ausgabe des Bezugstextes: J. Osternacher, Theoduli eclogam recensuit et prolegomenis instruxit, Urfahr 1902, S. 30\endash 54. Walther I Nr. 664. Zu \ldblquote Ecloga Theodoli\rdblquote  vgl. VL\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  Bd. 9, Sp. 760\endash 764. Ed. des Kommentars: \u193 \'c1. P. Orb\u225 \'e1n, Anonymi Teutonici commentum in Theodoli eclogam e codice Utrecht, U.B. 292 editum (1), in: Vivarium 11, 1973, S. 5\endash 42, hier 5\endash 31 (Text stellenweise abweichend); bibliographische Angaben zu weiteren Teilen der Edition vgl. in: VL\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Bd. 9, Sp. 764. B. Nye Quinn, ps. Theodolus, in: Catalogus translationum et commentariorum: Mediaeval and renaissance Latin translations and commentaries, Bd. 2, Washington 1971, S. 398 ff. \endash  199\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 206\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  leer. 
