\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 165\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 170\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Excerpta varia ascetica\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Nota: Verbositas novem mala ingerit homini. Primum est, quod homo veritatem tenere non potest \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 novum est, quod plures dulces gracias amittit. Unde ait Catho: Virtutem primam puto conpescere linguam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Ps.-Cato, Disticha 1,3; Walther II Nr. 33716. (165\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 166\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) [\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Thomas a Kempis: Hospitale pauperum\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 ]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , cap. 17 und 18. (165\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Cap. 17. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De utilitate oracionis. Apud me oracio \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... [Ps 41,9]. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ubicumque fueris, assit tecum sancta oracio pro socio et solacio \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et in fine eius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: Opera omnia, Bd. 4, Freiburg 1918, S. 231 f. (165\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 166\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Cap. 18. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De privatis oracionibus quasi iaculis acutis in hostes.< Verbo domini \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... [Ps 32,6]. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Verbum dei scutum anime fidelis ad protegendum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ponere in domino spem meam\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: ebd., S. 232\endash 234. (166\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 169\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >Quomodo noviter conversi ad deum temptantur.< Scire debes, quod per penitenciam et conversionem ad deum multa retrahere solent impedimenta \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ut possumus sustinere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (169\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 170\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 D\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 e timore dei\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De timore.< Debes scire, quod prima virtus et per quam pervenitur ad alias virtutes, est timor domini \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 caritatis perfectio possidetur. >Hec Cassianus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .< Genannte Autoren und Quellen: Biblia, Ambrosius, Basilius, Bernardus, Hieronymus, Isidorus, Johannes Cassianus, \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Glosa\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . Anschlie\u223 \'dfend: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Interroga teipsum, o homo, ut videas, quid interroganti deo respondere possis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ut sciatur, quantus locus tibi in celo debeatur. Hec ex vita domini. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Exzerpt aus Ludolphus de Saxonia: Vita Iesu Christi (pars 1, cap. 19). Druck: Ludolphus the Carthusian: Vita Christi, Bd. 2, Paris u.a. 1865 (Nachdruck Salzburg 2006) (Analecta Cartusiana, 241), S. 91. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Dicebat Anthonius: Qui sedet in solitudine \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 sicut dominus coram preside.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 171\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 175\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Thomas a Kempis: Doctrinale iuvenum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >Incipit libellus, qui dicitur doctrinale iuvenum, fratris Thome Kempis ordinis canonicorum regularium de recommendatione sacre scripture. Capitulum primum.< Fili, a iuventute \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... [Sir 6,18]. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Igitur ante omnes artes disce sacram scripturam legere \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 per eterna secula seculorum. Amen. >Finit.< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash  Druck: Opera omnia, Bd. 4, Freiburg 1918, S. 181\endash 199. U. Bodemann-Kornhaas, Die Kleineren Werke ... (vgl. Bl. 105\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ), S. 147 (Hs. genannt).}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 175\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 188\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Thomas a Kempis: Hortulus rosarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >Incipit libellus eiusdem, qui dicitur Ortulus rosarum. De bona societate querenda et mala fugienda. Capitulum 1.< Cum sancto sanctus eris \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... [Ps 17,26\endash 27]. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Attende diligenter, frater amande in Christo, ne seducaris a sociis malivolis, dissolutis et mendosis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 deo sic conclude. Deo gracias, deo laus, nunc et in eternum. Omnis spiritus laudet dominum. Amen. >Explicit libellus, qui dicitur Ortulus rosarum.< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash  Druck: P. van Geest, Thomas a Kempis (1379/80\endash 1471). Een studie van zijn mens- en godsbeeld. Analyse en tekstuitgave van de \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Hortulus rosarum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 en de \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Vallis liliorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , Kampen 1996, S. 343\endash 381 (unter Verwendung dieser Hs. [Sigle \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ds\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ]; Beschreibung der Hs. S. 297 ff.; weitere Nennung S. 337:); Opera omnia, Bd. 4, Freiburg 1918, S. 3\endash 50. Bloomfield/Guyot Nr. 1214 mit Suppl. U. Bodemann-Kornhaas, Die Kleineren Werke ... (vgl. Bl. 105\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ), S. 129 (Hs. genannt). Text \u252 \'fcberliefert auch in Ms. B 185, 78\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 188\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 194\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Thomas a Kempis: Dialogus novitiorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , lib. 1. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >Incipit prologus eiusdem devoti fratris in dyalogum noviciorum.< Colligite, que superaverunt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... [Io 6,12]\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 . Verbum Christi est ad discipulos suos \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 amplius accendantur. >Explicit prologus. Incipit dyalogus noviciorum de contemptu mundi.< Novicius: Rogo te, pater karissime, ut amore Ihesu Christi diligentem ad me respectum habeas \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et invenietis requiem animabus vestris. Quam nobis prestare dignetur Ihesus Christus, Marie filius, qui regnavit deus p\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (er) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 o\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (mnia) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 s\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (ecula) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 s\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (eculorum)\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 . Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: Opera omnia, Bd. 7, Freiburg 1922, S. 1\endash 30 (ohne den letzten Abschnitt). Bloomfield/Guyot Nr. 859 und 5215. Perger Nr. 129.1. U. Bodemann-Kornhaas, Die Kleineren Werke ... (vgl. Bl. 105\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ), S. 152 (Hs. genannt).}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 194\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 195\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Thomas a Kempis]: Consolatio pauperum et infirmorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit consolatio pauperum et infirmorum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Consolamini, consolamini \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... [Is 40,1]. >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Pauper.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Noli pauper tristari, quia dives non es \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 pro victoria consummata\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: Opera omnia, Bd. 4, Freiburg 1918, S. 137\endash 140. U. Bodemann-Kornhaas, Die Kleineren Werke ... (vgl. Bl. 105\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ), S. 146 (Hs. genannt). Anschlie\u223 \'dfend Exzerpt aus: [\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Thomas a Kempis: Epistula ad quendam cellerarium]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , cap. 3, Exzerpt. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >Quis sit aptus divinis colloquiis.< Juvat valde pro adipiscenda crebra domini amicicia \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 experiri solacia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: Opera omnia, Bd. 1, Freiburg 1910, S. 187.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 195\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 196\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 Thomas a Kempis: Epistula ad quendam a ministerio suo absolutum de recommendatione solitudinis et custodia silentii\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ], cap. 1 und 2, Exzerpte. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >Consolatio spiritualis hominis.< Qui ad tantam graciam pervenire potest \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 a proposito suo retrahunt. >Signa devotorum.< Bonum signum devotionis est cellam amare \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ad exercicia spiritualia. >Temptaciones devotorum.< Forte aliter interdum secum experiuntur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (196\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ad eternam vitam. >Reprobatio temporalis solacii.< Quid potest boni conferre homini \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 mirifica adimplebit. >De familiaritate cum Ihesu.< Quere igitur ipsius ditari consolatione \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 quid iam deesse poterit? >De laude pacientis adversa cum Ihesu.< Quam laudabilis hic \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (196\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 in paciente vere dileccio. >De solacio habendo cum Christo Ihesu.< Hic itaque pro solacio unico tibi sit, ubicumque fueris \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Christum libenter derelinquit. >Silendum est magis devotis temporibus et festivitatibus.< Bene deceret religiosum quibusdam devotis temporibus anni \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 magno gaudioque sincero suscipere. >Cur non suscipimus fructum ex frequenti communione.< Timendum, quod ideo multi fructum parvum accipiunt \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ad susceptionem eius\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: Opera omnia, Bd. 4, Freiburg 1918, S. 401\endash 445, hier S. 408, 409\endash 411, 413\endash 414, 437 f. und 441. U. Bodemann-Kornhaas, Die Kleineren Werke ... (vgl. Bl. 105\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ), S. 136 (Hs. genannt).}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 197\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 207\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 [Johannes de Castello]\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 : De fine religiosae perfectionis (De adhaerendo deo)\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >Incipit liber Alberti Magni de adherendo deo nudato intellectu et affectu et summa perfectione hominis, quantum possibile est. Primum capittulum.< Cogitanti michi aliquid ultimate, in quantum possibile est in huius exilii et peregrinacionis immoracione, depingere \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 a qua nos custodiat Ihesus Christus. Amen\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: Albertus Magnus, Opera omnia, Bd. 37, Paris 1898, S. 523\endash 534. Bloomfield/Guyot Nr. 842 mit Suppl.; Hamesse/Szyller Nr. 7684. J. Sudbrack, Die geistliche Theologie des Johannes von Kastl. Studien zur Fr\u246 \'f6mmigkeitsgeschichte des Sp\u228 \'e4tmittelalters, Teil 2, M\u252 \'fcnster 1966 (Beitr\u228 \'e4ge zur Geschichte des alten M\u246 \'f6nchtums und des Benediktinerordens; 27,2), S. 299 (Hs. genannt).}

