\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 222\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 [Ps.-Bonaventura]: Exercitia quaedam spiritualia\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , Exzerpt. <\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 U\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 t in virtutibus conserveris, oportet te habere exercicia spiritualia \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 nichil potes facere. Et sic est finis exerciciorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck:\~GW 4648. Bloomfield/Guyot Nr. 6215 mit Suppl.; Glorieux, R\u233 \'e9pertoire, Nr. 305bm; Distelbrink Nr. 133.}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 222\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 231\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 [Jacobus de Paradiso: Oculus religiosorum]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , Exzerpte. (222\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 224\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De curiositate.< Quia ex suspicione oriri solet curiositas \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 sed per illam ad istam tendant\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (224\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 225\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De propria voluntate et inobediencia.< Sciendum quod primum ostium cuiuslibet religiosi debet esse obediencia per remotionem proprie voluntatis et inobediencie \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et turbacio inobedientis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (225\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 226\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De consuetudinaria operacione.< Hostis eciam antiquus, omnium bonorum inimicus, inpellere solet mentes religiosorum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 totum corpus lucidum erit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (226\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 228\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De irreverencia circa altaris sacramentum.< Ex qua consuetudinaria operacione una eciam non minima pullulare creditur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 superaddere consueverant\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (228\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 231\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De corde seculari.< Aliud iterum occurrit, quod seminator zizaniorum in cordibus religiosorum noctis medie \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 si non segniter inchoetur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  L. Meier, Die Werke ..., s.o., S. 42, Nr. 45; D. Mertens, Iacobus Carthusiensis, s.o., S. 36 (zur Datierung des Werkes). Verglichen mit Ms. theol. lat. fol. 710, Staatsbibliothek zu Berlin \endash  Preu\u223 \'dfischer Kulturbesitz, 15\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 53\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .}

{\rtf1\ansi\ansicpg0\uc1\deff0\deflang0\deflangfe0{\fonttbl{\f0\fnil\fcharset1 Arial;}{\f1\fnil\fcharset0 Times New Roman;}}{\colortbl;\red0\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;\red0\green255\blue255;\red0\green255\blue0;\red255\green0\blue255;\red255\green0\blue0;\red255\green255\blue0;\red255\green255\blue255;\red0\green0\blue128;\red0\green128\blue128;\red0\green128\blue0;\red128\green0\blue128;\red128\green0\blue0;\red128\green128\blue0;\red128\green128\blue128;\red192\green192\blue192;\red204\green238\blue221;}

\uc1
\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 231\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 243\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  [\plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 David de Augusta: De exterioris et interioris hominis compositione]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 , lib. 2 und 3 (Exzerpte). (231\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 232\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De tribus, que vicia expellunt.< Tria sunt, que vicia in nobis expellunt et virtutes operantur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 vel aggredi non presumunt\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: Fr. David ab Augusta O.F.M., De exterioris et interioris hominis compositione, Quaracchi 1899, S. 116\endash 119. (232\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De remediis superbie.< Primum superbie remedium est consideracio proprie vilitatis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 tam in faciendo bona quam paciendo adversa\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: ebd., S. 122\endash 124 (Text gek\u252 \'fcrzt). (232\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 233\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De remediis invidie.< Primum remedium contra invidiam est, quod eciam summum est, nichil amare \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 sed non prevalebunt. Exemplum in sanctis martyribus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: ebd., S. 126\endash 128 (stellenweise gek\u252 \'fcrzt). (233\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De remediis ire.< Primum remedium ire est provida premeditacio illorum, que possunt occurrere \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et impaciencie facilius superamus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (233\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 234\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De accidia.< Accidie vicium tres habet species \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et redimamus tempus, quod male amisimus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (234\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De remediis accidie.< Primum et efficacius remedium accidie est cogere se ad ea spiritualia studia \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 equo animo sustinere\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: ebd., S. 129\endash 136. (234\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 235\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De remediis gule.< Gula secundum tradicionem seniorum prima est pugna \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et iusticia proximos persequuntur\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: ebd., S. 141\endash 146 (Text gek\u252 \'fcrzt). (235\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 236\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De remediis luxurie.< Remedia luxurie sunt septem \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 ignem concupiscencie\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: ebd., S. 151\endash 159 (Text gek\u252 \'fcrzt). (236\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 237\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De speciebus temptacionum.< Multe sunt temptacionum species \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 desiderium devocionis germinet\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck:\~ebd., S. 172\endash 178. (237\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 238\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De remediis contra temptaciones.< Contra tales temptaciones ista maxime valent remedia \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Secundum multitudinem dolorum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [Ps 93,19]. \endash  Druck: vgl.\~ebd., S. 180 f. und S. 190 f. (238\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De rectitudine actionis.< Actio in tribus debet esse circumspecta \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et amara carpet et nociva\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (238\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 239\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De rectitudine locutionis.< In locutione tria sunt similiter observanda \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 gloriam meretur in celo. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (239\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De disciplina morum.< Morum disciplina in religiosis triplici colore decoratur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 maturitas venerabilem\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: ebd., S. 192\endash 198. \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De paciencia.< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (239\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Paciencia est eterne glorie respectu voluntaria \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et gloriam in futuro\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: ebd., S. 251 f. (239\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 240\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >Ad quid valeat paciencia.< Valet autem virtus paciencie ad multa \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 eciam proprius conregnabit\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: ebd., S. 254\endash 257. (240\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De sobrietate.< Sobrietas est virtus, qua corporis alimenta cum moderamine admittuntur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et secundum deum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: ebd., S. 276 f. (240\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 241\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >De tribus, in quibus consistit sobrietas.< Sobrietas in tribus consistit: in qualitate, quantitate et modo \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et illic celestibus deliciis habundabimus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: ebd., S. 278 f. (241\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De communibus quibusdam spiritualibus exerciciis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .< \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Ad evitandum apostatice prevaricationis obprobrium \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 sanitatem virtutis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (241\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De agilitate ad incipiendum bonum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .< \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Primum est, ut homo sit inpiger et agilis ad incipiendum et faciendum bonum \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 vel cuiuslibet alterius virtutis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (241\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De velocitate se abstrahendi a malis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .< \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Secundum, ut, sicut ad agenda bona agilis, ita sit ad abstrahendum se velox a quibusdam malis \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 cor pacificum cum omnibus\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (241\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 242\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De pace cordis\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .< \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Tercium est, ut semper cor pacificum cum omnibus habere studeamus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Luce: In paciencia vestra possi\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (debitis) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 etc. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 [Lc 21,19]. (242\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De parcitate utendi, que mundi sunt.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Quartum, ut, quanto parcius potest, quis, que sunt mundi, utatur \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 in celo dilatabuntur et econverso\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (242\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rv\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De humili estimacione.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Quintum est, ut semper et intus apud se et extra coram hominibus se humiliet \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 tantum erramus a veritate\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . (242\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De maturitate et seriositate\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .< \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Sextum est, ut sit maturus et seriosus \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 maxime ioculari. \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (242\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 v\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 243\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 r\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 De suspensione mentis in deum.\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 < \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Septimum est mentem semper habere ad deum suspensam orando \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 et vias quam cogitacio terrenorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \endash  Druck: ebd., S. 203\endash 214 (stellenweise gek\u252 \'fcrzt). \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >Hec ex profectibus religiosorum breviter scripta sunt.< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 Zum Text vgl. CALMA Bd. 3,1, S. 66 f., Nr. 1.}

