\pard\fi0\li0\ql\ri0\sb0\sa0\itap0 \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 33\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 112\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  \plain \f1\scaps\lang1033\fs26 [Henricus Arnoldi: Dialogus de perfectione caritatis]\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 . \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 >Tractatus de modo perveniendi ad veram et perfectam dei et proximi dilectionem habens fundamentum ex theologia mistica. Et licet sit pro religiosis et aliis devocioni deditis, multum utilis potest nichilominus deservire et ceteris catholice fidei professoribus, cum omnes ad dilectionem dei et proximi teneamur. Editus a quodam cartusiensi ad dei laudem et aliorum edificationem. Incipit prologus in eandem materiam.< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (33\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 34\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Prolog: \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Caritas excellentissima satis in divino commendatur eloquio \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... (34\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 ra\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 35\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Tabula capitulorum\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 .< (35\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash 112\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 rb\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) Text: >\plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Incipit de caritate materia. Caritatis lex ut in corde scribatur, petitur. Capitulum 1.< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 (35\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 va\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ) \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 Amator meus, amor meus, amantissime, amabilissime domine Ihesu Christe \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 \endash  \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 ... \plain \f1\i\lang1033\fs26 desideramus et petimus. Et ignosce presumptioni. >Explicit dyalogus domini de caritate.< \plain \f1\lang1033\fs26 \endash  Druck: GW 2511 (hier wahrscheinlich Abschrift dieses Druckes, vgl. CCCM 121A, S. 387); Dionysius Cartusianus, Opera omnia, Bd. 41, Tournai 1912, S. 347\endash 417; Bibliotheca ascetica 1723/24, Bd. 6, ed. B. Pez (Repr. 1967), S. 1 ff. Bloomfield/Guyot Nr. 375 mit Suppl. Dionysii Cartusiensis Opera selecta, Bd. 1: K. Emery, Prolegomena: Bibliotheca manuscripta; IB: Studia bibliographica, Turnhout 1991 (= CCCM 121A; Hs. genannt S. 379 und 386 f.); Perger Nr. 157.1; VL\plain \f1\super\lang1033\fs24 2\plain \f1\lang1033\fs26  Bd. 1, Sp. 488; LMA Bd. 4, Sp. 2136.}

